 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "The proof already exists twice inline: line 138 `rw [coeff_one_subst G.constantCoeff_toPowerSeries, smul_eq_mul]` in the `Mul` instance, and line 194 `simp [coeff_one_subst G.constantCoeff_toPowerSeries]` in `linearCoeff`'s `map_mul'`. Reading the full file shows `coeff_one_toPowerSeries_inv` is the only `coeff_one_toPowerSeries_*` lemma. `Mathlib/RingTheory/PowerSeries/Basic.lean:226` confirms `@[simp] coeff_one_X`, which covers the `1` case but not `*`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/RingTheory/PowerSeries/Substitution.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] lemma coeff_one_toPowerSeries_mul (F G : SubstGroup R) : coeff 1 (F * G).toPowerSeries = coeff 1 F.toPowerSeries * coeff 1 G.toPowerSeries`, proved by `rw [toPowerSeries_mul, coeff_one_subst G.constantCoeff_toPowerSeries, smul_eq_mul]`, and use it in the `Mul` instance and in `linearCoeff.map_mul'`.",
   "issue": "`coeff 1 (F * G).toPowerSeries` has no lemma and no simp normal form: `@[simp] toPowerSeries_mul` rewrites it to `coeff 1 (F.toPowerSeries.subst G.toPowerSeries)`, and `coeff_one_subst` is not `@[simp]`, so simp stalls there. The interaction of `coeff 1` with `\u207b\u00b9` is given (`@[simp] coeff_one_toPowerSeries_inv`, line 204) and with `1` (via `toPowerSeries_one` + Mathlib's `@[simp] coeff_one_X`), but the product case \u2014 the group's defining operation \u2014 is missing. This matters downstream because every scheme-change theorem in BetaFunction.lean is gated on `coeff 1 F.toPowerSeries = 1` (`betaCoeff_transformBeta_zero_of_coeff_one_eq_one` etc.) while `transformBeta_mul` is the API for composing redefinitions, so discharging the hypothesis for a composite requires a manual detour through `mem_ker_linearCoeff_iff` and `Subgroup.mul_mem`.",
   "line": 150
  }
 ],
